On $[0,\pi]$, the input is already in the range of inverse cosine, so $y=x$. On $[\pi,2\pi]$, the equivalent angle is $2\pi-x$. Cosine is even and repeats every $2\pi$, giving the remaining segments.
$y=\begin{cases}-x,&-\pi\le x\le0,\\x,&0\le x\le\pi,\\2\pi-x,&\pi\le x\le2\pi,\\x-2\pi,&2\pi\le x\le3\pi.\end{cases}$
